              "text": "The iconic American **Spiegel catalog and its online store (spiegel.com) are no longer active**. \n\n### What Happened to Spiegel?\nFounded in 1865, Spiegel was a staple of American mail-order shopping for over a century, famous for its fashionable clothing, home decor, and European-inspired designs. After facing financial struggles in the early 2000s, the brand transitioned from a print catalog to a digital-only online retailer. \n\nHowever, in **2019**, the company officially ceased operations, and the website was taken down without notice. \n\n### Avoid Common Online Confusions\nIf you have been searching for Spiegel online, you may have run into a few misleading results:\n* **\"Spiegel 2026 Catalog\" listings:** Catalog directory sites like *Catalogs.com* still host pages titled \"Spiegel 2026 Catalog.\" These are purely historical placeholder pages or landing pages redirecting you to alternative brands; **there is no active Spiegel catalog to order or shop from.**\n* **\"Spiegel & More\" or other \"Spiegel\" home sites:** Because *\"Spiegel\"* is the German word for *\"mirror,\"* you may see active home decor websites with \"Spiegel\" in the name (such as European mirror manufacturers). These are completely unrelated to the historic Chicago-based mail-order retailer.\n\n---\n\n### Where to Shop Instead (Best Alternatives)\nIf you loved the elegant, classic style of Spiegel\u2019s home and fashion offerings, there are several active catalog and online retailers that capture a very similar vibe:\n\n#### For Home Decor, Bedding, and Furnishings:\n* **Garnet Hill:** Excellent for high-quality bedding, fine linens, and home decor that match the sophisticated quality Spiegel was known for.\n* **Ballard Designs:** Offers a classic, European-influenced aesthetic for furniture, tableware, and home accents.\n* **Grandin Road:** Known for vibrant, upscale, and transitional home furnishings and seasonal decor. \n* **Plow & Hearth / Country Door:** Great options if you enjoyed the warm, traditional, and cozy side of Spiegel's home collections.\n\n#### For Women\u2019s Fashion (The Spiegel & Newport News Vibe):\n* **Boston Proper:** If you loved Spiegel's younger, sun-drenched sister brand, *Newport News*, Boston Proper is the closest match for chic, contemporary, and travel-ready clothing.\n* **Talbots:** The best active match for the upscale, tailored, and classic look of Spiegel\u2019s legacy catalogs.\n* **Soft Surroundings:** Focuses on casual luxury, relaxed fits, and high-quality fabrics.\n\n*If you are feeling nostalgic, you can still find vintage print Spiegel catalogs (as well as vintage Spiegel clothing and home goods) from collectors on **eBay** and **Etsy**.*",
